From: Zomdroid
Subject: [PATCH] glapi: export the GL_ARB_timer_query entry points statically

libzfa.so links libglapi_static whole and has no GetProcAddress, so LWJGL resolves every GL
function by name. A function is a static export only if it is listed in static_data.functions,
and the three GL_ARB_timer_query functions (core in OpenGL 3.3) are not: glQueryCounter,
glGetQueryObjecti64v and glGetQueryObjectui64v resolved to NULL, and PZ3D killed the JVM on its
first glQueryCounter call although the context reports OpenGL 4.6. Offsets are unchanged; only the
export list grows. They are the only core functions up to OpenGL 3.3 missing from the list.

---
diff --git a/src/mapi/glapi/gen/static_data.py b/src/mapi/glapi/gen/static_data.py
--- a/src/mapi/glapi/gen/static_data.py
+++ b/src/mapi/glapi/gen/static_data.py
@@ -2180,8 +2180,10 @@
     "GetQueryIndexediv",
     "GetQueryiv",
     "GetQueryivARB",
+    "GetQueryObjecti64v",
     "GetQueryObjectiv",
     "GetQueryObjectivARB",
+    "GetQueryObjectui64v",
     "GetQueryObjectuiv",
     "GetQueryObjectuivARB",
     "GetRenderbufferParameteriv",
@@ -2535,6 +2537,7 @@
     "PushDebugGroup",
     "PushMatrix",
     "PushName",
+    "QueryCounter",
     "RasterPos2d",
     "RasterPos2dv",
     "RasterPos2f",
